  "description": "GEZJIG crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C92 H96 Dy10 N30 O24. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy5A (Dy) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 23 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.504-4.136 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.55-127.96°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy10(bpt)6(μ4-O)4(μ3-OMe)4(μ-OMe)8(μ-OAc)2(OAc)2]·40H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
